# mutants-round2.log — evidence that the round-2 F5 regression test can FAIL.
#
# Verifier round 2, finding 2: the round-2 test asserted two strings and passed on the
# defect it was written for. These two mutants are the proof that the replacement
# discriminates. A regression test that has never failed on its defect is not evidence.
#
#   mutantA  delete ONLY `cd "$REPO"`; the pre-flight guards left intact.
#            --screen exits 1, and --self-test now FAILS with 3 assertions.
#   mutantB  delete `cd "$REPO"` AND the pre-flight guards — the true round-1 shape.
#            --screen exits 1, and --self-test FAILS with 2 assertions.
#
# Mutants are built in a scratch COPY; the real worktree is never modified.
# Every absolute path is replaced with <SCRATCH>: a committed transcript must carry no
# home path (AGENTS.md §7), and the failure messages quote mktemp directories verbatim.
# Re-derive by re-running the mutant build described in FINDINGS.md §8.

